# Local tool artifacts — knowledge-graph / agent DB state, churns every session
ruvector.db
# graphify: the graph itself stays out (graph.json is 16MB and is rewritten in full on every
# build; cache/ and the HTML are derived). The markdown layer IS committed on purpose: cloud and
# web agents cannot run the graphify CLI, so wiki/ and GRAPH_REPORT.md are the only artifacts
# they can actually read. Needs `graphify-out/*`, not `graphify-out/`, because git cannot
# re-include a child once its parent directory is excluded.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/wiki/
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
agentdb*.rvf
agentdb*.rvf*.lock
agentdb*.lock
.swarm/

# Agent skills installed via the skills CLI. The manifest skills-lock.json IS committed
# (reproducible source of truth); the installed content (.agents/, ~2MB of third-party
# skills from vercel-labs / Panniantong) and the .claude/skills/* symlinks that point into
# it are the node_modules-equivalent — rebuild them by re-running the installer, never vendor.
.agents/
.claude/skills/agent-reach
.claude/skills/deploy-to-vercel
.claude/skills/vercel-cli-with-tokens
.claude/skills/vercel-composition-patterns
.claude/skills/vercel-optimize
.claude/skills/vercel-react-best-practices
